# Implementation scope

## First proof (M1)

Build the **13-step autonomous vertical slice** defined in `docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md`:

1. Objective → 2. Delegation → 3. Real external research → 4. Source-backed knowledge → 5. Falsifiable hypothesis → 6. Historical data → 7. Isolated strategy execution → 8. Reproducible backtest → 9. Independent validation → 10. Reflection → 11. Lessons stored → 12. Next experiment proposed → 13. Resume after interruption

## Prefer

- Thin packages on the critical path: core, schemas, data, research, validation, agents/comm, scheduler
- Postgres outbox + explicit FSM
- BTC/ETH spot + perps only
- CLI timeline acceptable if dashboard lags

## Defer / reject for M1

- Live capital, multi-agent debate UIs, Neo4j, Kubernetes-heavy prod topology
- PyTorch/RL/evolutionary search as default alpha path
- Orchestration frameworks without a benchmark beating the FSM
- Portfolio management until ≥1 validated path exists (or explicit single-strategy paper policy in M2)

## Workstream contracts

Integrate via published interfaces in IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN §2. Do not invent cross-plane shortcuts to “make the demo work.”
